Z||000000||v8vinnie||12-24-2000||05:36 PM||||HI, my name is vincent was woundering if any body can tell me if i install poly bushings in the cradle and controlarm would be too harsh on the street, i live in florida and i have owned 3 corvettes and want this 1987gt handle as good as the 345hp zz3 chevy crate motor goes, gets pretty hairy in turnes on the throttle and from my feeling its deffenitly bushing deflection, so far i have put kyb strunts on rear any thoughts||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||12-24-2000||06:48 PM||||(I gather) your first move should be to replace the cradle bushings with poly or solid metal bushings.  Much easier/ less downtime than control arm bushings.  Try that, see how you like it, and go from there.<P>Just paraphrasing what I've read here on the forum.   ||||reg||1
Z||000002||bHooper||12-24-2000||06:55 PM||||i just replaced every bushing in my car with poly.  now its been cold, damp and dreary, and i have old tires, so i haven't pushed the car hard, yet.  but it's very tight and feels good.<P>do a search for nopi and poly bushings to get the part numbers, and prices.  they are much cheaper from there!<P>good luck!<P>hoop||||reg||14
